+1

5. Unnamed Patterns and Variables — Preview in Java 21
=======================================================
Problem before: Sometimes we need to match a value but do not need to use it.

Before:

if (obj instanceof String value) {
    System.out.println("It is a String");
}

Here, value is declared but never used.

Java 21 preview syntax:

if (obj instanceof String _) {
    System.out.println("It is a String");
}

The underscore _ indicates an unnamed variable or pattern.

Why useful? It makes code cleaner when a matched value is not needed.

Interview answer: “Java 21 previewed unnamed patterns and variables, allowing us to ignore values that are not required.”

This was a preview feature, not a permanent Java 21 feature. 
