6. Unnamed Classes and Instance Main Methods — Preview in Java 21
=================================================================
Before: Even a simple Java program required a class declaration and a main method.

public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        System.out.println("Hello Java");
    }
}

Java 21 preview syntax:

void main() {
    System.out.println("Hello Java");
}

Why useful? It makes Java easier for beginners to start learning without introducing every class-related concept immediately.

Interview answer: “Java 21 previewed unnamed classes and instance main methods to simplify writing small Java programs.”

This was also a preview feature in Java 21, not a permanent feature. 
