7. String Templates — Preview in Java 21
========================================
Problem before: We commonly used string concatenation or String.format().

Before:

String name = "Riya";
int age = 25;

String message = "Name: " + name + ", Age: " + age;

Another option:

String message = String.format(
        "Name: %s, Age: %d", name, age
);

Java 21 introduced a preview of string templates using syntax like this:

String name = "Riya";
int age = 25;

// Java 21 preview syntax
String message = STR."Name: \{name}, Age: \{age}";

Why useful? It provides a more readable way to combine literal text with expressions.

Important: String templates were previewed in Java 21 and later withdrawn from the language design. Do not present this syntax as a standard, finalized Java 21 feature for production code. 
