8. Generational ZGC — Java 21
==============================
Problem before: Garbage collection can affect application responsiveness, particularly in applications with many objects and strict latency requirements.

Java 21 enhanced the Z Garbage Collector (ZGC) with a generational mode.

java -XX:+UseZGC -XX:+ZGenerational MyApplication

What does generational mean?

The garbage collector separates objects into generations, typically based on whether they are young or old.

Young objects are often short-lived and can be collected frequently.

Old objects tend to survive longer and can be managed separately.

Why useful? Generational ZGC aims to reduce garbage-collection overhead and improve performance for suitable workloads.

Interview answer: “Java 21 introduced generational mode for ZGC, allowing young and old objects to be managed separately to improve garbage-collection efficiency.” 
